// Title: ImagingDevices Unusual Parent/Child Processes
// Sigma ID: f11f2808-adb4-46c0-802a-8660db50fa99
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-27 | Modified: 2022-12-29
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth
// Description: Detects unusual parent or children of the ImagingDevices.exe (Windows Contacts) process as seen
//   being used with Bumblebee activity
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://thedfirreport.com/2022/09/26/bumblebee-round-two/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_imagingdevices_unusual_parents.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\WmiPrvSE.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\svchost.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\dllhost.exe") and FolderPath endswith "\\ImagingDevices.exe") or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\ImagingDevices.exe"
